 on JOE MCDONALD","note":"distance runner and Club Champion; bests include marathon 2hr 46min 06sec (Poly Marathon 1952) and London - Brighton 6hr 38min 20sec (1952); in his latter 50s in 1977; born in Kensington June 2nd 1921; schoolboy at Beaufort House; Church Lads Brigade; joined Belgrave November 2nd 1938; won five mile cross country handicap October 1947; first Polytechnic Marathon 1948 in 3 hours 17 minutes 1 second; ran fourteen consecutive Poly marathons, last in 1961; 29th and first Belgrave home in the 1952 Polytechnic Marathon (Olympic trial), 2 hours 46 minutes 6 seconds, earning a Club Championship and Honours Badge; 16th in the first Road Runners Club London to Brighton run, August 27th 1952; R.R.C. 2nd class award 1954; made a Vice-President in 1972"},{"id":"B195-70","when":"October 1977","p":44,"h":"MAY 7th 1977 - RICHMOND PARK - VETERANS AC 10 MILE ROAD CHAMP.","note":"54th, 64:50"},{"id":"B195-93","when":"October 1977","p":55,"h":"... and again","note":"28th 19:55"},{"id":"B196-100","when":"April 1978","p":40,"h":"MARCH 11th 1978 - WIMBLEDON - 5¾ MILE CHAMPIONSHIP. A NEW CHAMPION","note":"36th 41:02; won handicap (15:30) 25:32"},{"id":"B196-62","when":"April 1978","p":27,"h":"from the Belgravian... ... 25 years ago: COUNTY SENIOR C.C. CHAMPIONSHIPS......1953"},{"id":"B196-66","when":"April 1978","p":28,"h":"SEPTEMBER 24th 1977 - WIMBLEDON - BELGRAVE 5¾ ROAD RACE."},{"id":"B197-23","when":"October 1978","p":17,"h":"100x1 mile relay","note":"stage 57 of 100 x 1 mile relay, 6:35"},{"id":"B197-81","when":"October 1978","p":40,"h":"Opposite page. The Philips 100x1 mile relay.","note":"in 100x1 mile relay photo"},{"id":"B198-32","when":"April 1979","p":15,"h":"Boxing Day Handicaps","note":"15th Mens 2 miles, 11:45"},{"id":"B198-38","when":"April 1979","p":19,"h":"OCTOBER 21st 1978 - WIMBLEDON - SURREY C.C. LEAGUE RACE 1.","note":"204th, 43:38"},{"id":"B198-40","when":"April 1979","p":19,"h":"A NIGHT OUT FOR JOE","note":"presented with a plaque for 40 ye